==English==

===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|en-us-holler.ogg|Audio (US)}}
*:Rhymes: [[Rhymes:English:-ɒlə(r)|-ɒlə(r)]]

===Etymology===
American variant of holla or [[hallo]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

#A [[yell]], [[shout]].
#:''I heard a '''holler''' from over the fence.''
#By extension, any communication to get somebody's attention.
#:''If you need anything, just give me a '''holler'''.''
#A rural road in the appalachians in the U.S.A.
#In South Midland and Southern (dialects of American English), a [[hollow]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

#To [[yell]] or [[shout]].
#:''You can '''holler''' at your computer as much as you want, but it won't help anything.''

#Under the subject of ghetto terminology, the act of "hollering" at someone or others has basically come to mean either getting in touch with them, reconciling a relationship, a request to "get back to me soon" or perhaps a simple "hello." One can "holler" at another in many different ways such as on the internet, phones, and face-to-face interaction. "Hollering" at someone has acted as a catalytic tool to communication and has allowed the steady growth of relationships. A request to "Holler" at one is almost always a positive sign to move forward; the term may almost always be used loosely. Copyright: Abie Boukai (I typed the above.)

